  "thought": "Construct routes using regret-insertion heuristic: for each unrouted customer, compute the insertion cost in the best position of each route, then identify the best and second-best route-level insertion costs. Regret is the difference between second-best and best. Insert the customer with the highest regret into its best position. This forces difficult customers to be placed early. After construction, improve by relocating customers from the longest route to shorter routes if it reduces the maximum route distance, and apply 2-opt within each route. All loops are bounded by the number of customers. Solutions are reported via report_best_vrp whenever a better maximum distance is found."
